# ABP Modular CRM Tutorial

Demonstrates building a modular monolith application with ABP.

## Key Concepts

### Module Structure
- Products module
- Ordering module
- Each module has its own:
  - Domain layer
  - Application layer
  - Database tables
  - UI pages

### Inter-Module Communication
- Use distributed event bus for module communication
- Modules are loosely coupled
- Can be extracted to microservices later

### Module Definition
```csharp
[DependsOn(typeof(ProductsDomainSharedModule))]
public class OrderingDomainModule : AbpModule
{
}
```

### Cross-Module Events
```csharp
// Publishing from Products module
await _distributedEventBus.PublishAsync(new ProductStockChangedEto
{
    ProductId = product.Id,
    NewStock = product.Stock
});

// Handling in Ordering module
public class ProductStockChangedHandler : IDistributedEventHandler<ProductStockChangedEto>
{
    public async Task HandleEventAsync(ProductStockChangedEto eventData)
    {
        // Handle stock change
    }
}
```
